{
  "//": "BUBBLE DROP - each tap releases one bubble from the spout. They fall, bounce and shove each other. Land all three in the bin before the clock runs out.",
  "//mechanic": "Bubbles push each other apart: each bubble computes a separation term against the other two and adds it to its own velocity. Three bubbles is the practical limit - each extra one costs every other bubble another term, and the expression cap is 32 tokens.",
  "//release": "The tap edge increments `drop`; bubble k is inert until drop reaches k, so one tap is one bubble and there are exactly three.",
  "//levels": "The bin narrows and moves, gravity rises and the clock tightens.",
